# Build output is committed to the `deploy` branch and served as-is. Next's RSC
# payloads under out/ contain literal CR bytes, and their internal length
# prefixes count them. Letting Git normalise line endings there silently drops
# those bytes, the stream then ends early, and client-side navigation dies with
# "Connection closed." — the visitor sees "This page couldn't load".
out/** -text

# Author markdown with LF regardless of platform. On a CRLF checkout the CRs
# inside fenced code blocks are preserved verbatim through the renderer and end
# up in the payload, which is how they reached out/ in the first place.
*.md text eol=lf
